  "about": "Innocent words and place names that contain a blocked term (Essex, Scunthorpe, Pakistan). They are taken out of a name before it is checked, so \"Essex Rising\" passes. Only whole words count: \"Essex\" is allowed, \"Essexsex\" is not. Lower-case letters, with a single space for a name of two words. After editing, run `npm run names` and re-run supabase/schema.sql in the Supabase SQL editor.",
